(function(){"use strict";window.EDMUND_DSE_LISTENING_2019_TRANSCRIPT=Object.freeze({"partA":{"1":[{"start":0,"end":6.66,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task 1. Sarah is meeting with Ms. Chan, the school principal,"},{"start":7.22,"end":13.8,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"and Ms. Reyes, a science teacher at the school, about the school's mobile phone use policy."},{"start":15.25,"end":20.01,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Listen to the discussion and write the information in the spaces below."},{"start":21.16,"end":24.04,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"The first one has been provided as an example."},{"start":25.41,"end":28.79,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have 30 seconds to study the task."},{"start":28.79,"end":33.93,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"At the end of the task, you will have one minute to tidy up your answers."},{"start":65.87,"end":67.59,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Good morning, Sarah. Come in."},{"start":68.23,"end":72.65,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"I thought it would be useful to have Ms. Reyes here as well to hear about your survey."},{"start":73.21,"end":74.69,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Good morning, Sarah. Hello!"},{"start":75.45,"end":83.17,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Okay, so as I was saying, Ms. Reyes, Sarah and her team at our IT club online magazine have been doing a survey"},{"start":83.17,"end":87.63,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"where they have been asking students about mobile phone use during the school day."},{"start":87.63,"end":91.05,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"So Sarah, maybe you can give us some more details."},{"start":92.01,"end":94.21,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Yes, and thank you for seeing me today."},{"start":94.93,"end":97.67,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Well, we're writing an article about the survey,"},{"start":98.15,"end":102.33,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"and we thought it would be good to include your comments as well in the article."},{"start":103.13,"end":103.83,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Okay, fine."},{"start":104.93,"end":110.89,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"The first issue we asked about was when we can use our phones during the school day."},{"start":111.74,"end":117.34,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"At the moment, we're only allowed to use our phones until 8.45 in the morning."},{"start":117.34,"end":120.54,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"And we can't use our phones during class."},{"start":121,"end":125.16,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Oh, I thought you could use your phones until 8.55."},{"start":126.02,"end":128.42,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"No, only until 8.45."},{"start":128.82,"end":130.24,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Okay, my mistake."},{"start":131.02,"end":133.98,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"So students think the policy is outdated."},{"start":135.02,"end":138.86,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"What do you mean by outdated? What would students like to change?"},{"start":139.46,"end":143.16,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Well, I think they'd like the policy to be more flexible."},{"start":143.16,"end":148.1,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"I see. And this is the feedback from the school survey you did."},{"start":148.74,"end":150.68,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Sorry, can you tell us more about it?"},{"start":151.1,"end":156.36,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Yes, we did a survey to ask students about why they want to use their phones,"},{"start":156.78,"end":158.92,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"and lots of students responded."},{"start":159.6,"end":165.54,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"We heard from 64 junior students and 150 senior students,"},{"start":165.98,"end":169.88,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"so that's 214 students in total."},{"start":169.88,"end":173.96,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"214? That's a lot of responses."},{"start":174.78,"end":177.34,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"I'm impressed. Well done to the IT club."},{"start":178.26,"end":181.3,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"What were the main requests from students from the survey then?"},{"start":181.84,"end":186.76,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Well, the most popular requests were that students would like to use their phones"},{"start":186.76,"end":192.3,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"for 30 minutes at lunchtime and when walking between classes."},{"start":193,"end":196.1,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Walking between classes? Absolutely not."},{"start":196.88,"end":198.62,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Students would never arrive on time."},{"start":198.62,"end":203.94,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Half an hour at lunchtime is fair, but certainly not between classes."},{"start":204.54,"end":206.68,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"There's just enough time and no more."},{"start":206.96,"end":209.12,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Oh, okay. What else?"},{"start":209.76,"end":213.88,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Oh yeah, they also said they'd like permission to use their phones"},{"start":213.88,"end":217.02,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"during physics and language classes."},{"start":217.52,"end":220.06,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Why during those classes specifically?"},{"start":220.9,"end":223.78,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Well, they'd like to use them in physics classes"},{"start":223.78,"end":226.34,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"so they can use calculator apps."},{"start":226.34,"end":231.4,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"And they want to use them in language classes for online dictionaries."},{"start":232.06,"end":235.28,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"They said they think this would be really helpful for their studies,"},{"start":236.16,"end":239.1,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"especially for students who are preparing for exams."},{"start":240,"end":242.34,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"What do you think about that idea, Miss Reyes?"},{"start":242.96,"end":247.08,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Hmm. I don't agree that you need them in physics classes."},{"start":248.18,"end":251.16,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Scientific calculators are better than phone calculators,"},{"start":251.42,"end":254.78,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"but yes, they could be useful in language classes."},{"start":254.78,"end":259.14,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"I think you're absolutely right about both points, Miss Reyes."},{"start":259.9,"end":262.48,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"There's no need to use phones during physics class,"},{"start":262.98,"end":266.9,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"but using them for online dictionaries is definitely a good idea."},{"start":267.62,"end":271.35,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Okay. Were there any other issues that came up from the survey?"},{"start":272.03,"end":274.17,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Yes, there was one other request."},{"start":275.11,"end":278.75,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Students aren't allowed to charge their phone batteries in classrooms,"},{"start":278.75,"end":282.89,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"so they'd like to ask for a battery charging station."},{"start":282.89,"end":287.21,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"A battery charging station. That's actually a good idea."},{"start":288.33,"end":291.81,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Interesting. We'd have to think carefully about where to put it."},{"start":292.33,"end":295.29,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Did they have any suggestions? The students, I mean."},{"start":295.69,"end":300.63,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Well, one place they said was, you know, in the corridor next to the playground."},{"start":301.53,"end":303.87,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Hmm. I'm not so sure about that."},{"start":304.43,"end":306.95,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"There could be problems with security with that."},{"start":307.51,"end":310.57,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Yes, I tend to agree with Miss Chan, I'm afraid."},{"start":311.41,"end":315.93,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"So that's out as a location then. But I still think it's a good idea."},{"start":317.06,"end":319.92,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Sarah, did you have another suggestion for a location?"},{"start":320.6,"end":322.16,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"The other one was the library."},{"start":322.88,"end":327.72,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Okay. Yeah, that might work. It's certainly popular at lunchtime."},{"start":328.46,"end":331.62,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Yeah, that's a good idea. We'll look into it definitely."},{"start":332.45,"end":336.85,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Ms Chan","text":"Okay. Well, I'll look forward to reading the article in the online magazine."},{"start":338.65,"end":341.17,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"That is the end of task one."},{"start":342.24,"end":345.52,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have one minute to tidy up your answers."}],"2":[{"start":0.02,"end":0.76,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task two."},{"start":2.67,"end":8.59,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Sarah is meeting with two other members of the IT club, Aaron and Rachel,"},{"start":8.93,"end":14.37,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"to discuss a new app that the school is going to promote to senior students."},{"start":15.86,"end":20.26,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Listen to the discussion and write the information in the spaces below."},{"start":20.26,"end":24.66,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"The first one has been provided as an example."},{"start":26.52,"end":29.44,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have 30 seconds to study the task."},{"start":30.58,"end":34.96,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"At the end of the task, you will have one minute to tidy up your answers."},{"start":67.05,"end":70.97,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"So we've been asked to give our views on this Mentor Mine app."},{"start":71.39,"end":73.07,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"You know, the one for senior students?"},{"start":73.59,"end":75.89,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"They want us to review it in the magazine."},{"start":76.73,"end":80.45,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"I've had it on my phone and I've been giving it a go over the weekend."},{"start":81.09,"end":82.25,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"What's it called?"},{"start":83.19,"end":85.77,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Mental Mine. Never heard of it."},{"start":86.17,"end":87.91,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Not mental. Mental!"},{"start":88.89,"end":93.09,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Let me show you. Wait a second till I find it on my phone."},{"start":94.13,"end":95.03,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Right, here it is."},{"start":95.27,"end":96.15,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Oh, okay."},{"start":96.75,"end":104.03,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Right, so it's an app and it helps you connect with other students from around the world."},{"start":104.53,"end":107.65,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"And so they help each other with things like homework and projects."},{"start":108.33,"end":112.09,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Oh, I've heard about this one. It's got really good reviews."},{"start":113.35,"end":116.09,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"So you're saying you can get help with projects with this?"},{"start":116.51,"end":118.55,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Yeah, that's the idea anyway."},{"start":119.05,"end":121.37,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Alright, so how do we get started?"},{"start":122.19,"end":123.37,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Can we have a look at the settings?"},{"start":124.01,"end":125.87,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Right, settings."},{"start":127.09,"end":129.73,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Right, here we go. You try it, Rachel."},{"start":130.47,"end":133.33,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Oh, okay. Right."},{"start":133.33,"end":137.91,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"So see the button with the head and the wheels. Press it."},{"start":139.43,"end":145.65,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Well, here you start by choosing your subjects, your levels for each subject and your modes."},{"start":146.39,"end":148.97,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"You can select any subjects you like."},{"start":149.53,"end":153.43,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Oh, right. So it looks like there are three starting levels."},{"start":154.39,"end":157.57,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Beginner, apprentice and guide."},{"start":157.57,"end":169.49,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"So presumably I'd select guide if I think I know like loads about a subject and beginner or apprentice if I don't."},{"start":169.93,"end":170.37,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Exactly."},{"start":171.27,"end":173.51,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"What about mode? What does that mean?"},{"start":174.19,"end":178.33,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Okay, well, press it. So you should see there are two modes."},{"start":179.03,"end":181.81,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"The first one is academic. See?"},{"start":182.33,"end":182.87,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Oh, yeah."},{"start":183.35,"end":186.17,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"You choose this one if you're preparing for an exam."},{"start":186.17,"end":191.25,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"The other one is hobby and it's for like personal interest only."},{"start":192.6,"end":200.12,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Personal interest? Oh, so presumably people can talk about a subject even if, say, they're not studying for an exam?"},{"start":201.06,"end":205.9,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"What's this one for? The one with the flag? Is that to choose my country?"},{"start":206.46,"end":209.4,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Let's try it. Right."},{"start":209.4,"end":216.1,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"So it looks like there are two settings here, country and type of school."},{"start":216.68,"end":218.48,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"But isn't it just for secondary schools?"},{"start":219.22,"end":227.8,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Yeah, it is. But there are different types of schools in different countries, like many Italian schools specialising just one area."},{"start":228.32,"end":236.04,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"So if Italian teenagers want to specialise in, say, sports coaching, they can choose a school for that subject."},{"start":236.46,"end":236.88,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Right."},{"start":237.68,"end":240.88,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"What's the clock for? Does it tell the time then?"},{"start":241.1,"end":244.9,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"No, no. This is what they call the office hours setting."},{"start":245.5,"end":246.66,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"You keeping up, Rachel?"},{"start":247.02,"end":256.08,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Yeah, yeah, right. Office hours. Ah, because you're like a professor sitting in your office. That's clever."},{"start":256.8,"end":260.56,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"So with this setting, you can choose your availability each day."},{"start":260.56,"end":271,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"You can set a maximum of two hours each weekday to ask and answer live questions and more on weekends, say, three to four hours."},{"start":271.62,"end":275.78,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"You should set your office hours to when you would normally be doing your homework."},{"start":276.56,"end":278.7,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Why do they recommend to set time, do you think?"},{"start":279.3,"end":287.06,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Well, I was thinking about this and I think the first reason is they want to help students develop good time management skills."},{"start":287.06,"end":293.44,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Yeah, I have no time management skills whatsoever. I'm such a deadline fighter."},{"start":293.84,"end":300.08,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Yeah, I know. And the other is that it's useful for other students to know exactly when you're available."},{"start":301.06,"end":307.76,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Because if they know your availability, then they know when you might be able to answer a question. Makes sense."},{"start":308.42,"end":312.96,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"So what are these? What are they? Balloons or something?"},{"start":312.96,"end":319.9,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Yeah, I have no idea why. Anyway, you click this button to go to your feedback settings."},{"start":320.66,"end":326.76,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"You see, each time you help someone, they can give you a vote and then write a message to say thanks."},{"start":327.56,"end":331.64,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"The more votes you get, the sooner you can move up to a higher level."},{"start":331.88,"end":337.76,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"OK. Yeah, it allows you to show or hide the number of votes you've got as well."},{"start":337.76,"end":346.88,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"OK. Oh, and I can show or hide the messages I've received from people. You know, the ones that I've helped. That's pretty cool."},{"start":347.26,"end":350.54,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Yeah, I know. I think it's pretty cool all round actually."},{"start":350.9,"end":352.06,"speaker":"Mentor app presenters","text":"Yeah, it looks useful."},{"start":354.21,"end":360.38,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"That is the end of task two. You now have one minute to tidy up your answers."},{"start":424.76,"end":424.8,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task three. Sarah, Rachel and Erin are choosing stories about the use of technology around the world to feature in the IT Club's online magazine."}],"3":[{"start":0,"end":12.85,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task three. Sarah, Rachel and Erin are choosing stories about the use of technology around the world to feature in the IT Club's online magazine."},{"start":14.68,"end":23.08,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Listen to the information and complete the notes below. You now have 30 seconds to study the task."},{"start":24.11,"end":28.59,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"At the end of the task, you will have one minute to tidy up your answers."},{"start":28.59,"end":63.87,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Right. So what stories have you found then, Rachel?"},{"start":65,"end":75.08,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"OK, I'll go first. I was reading this interesting article about youth boost centres in South Africa that have been set up by the local government."},{"start":76,"end":79.88,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"OK, so these youth boost centres, are they for teenagers?"},{"start":80.52,"end":87.14,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Yeah, mainly for young people without a job and who aren't at college and they join the centre as members."},{"start":87.8,"end":89.16,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"So why do they sign up?"},{"start":89.16,"end":99.88,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Well, they can learn loads of different things like the centres give them lots of practical advice on things like how to start their own companies."},{"start":100.58,"end":107.88,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Sounds good. I've always wanted to start my own company. I think I'd like that much more than a boring office job or something."},{"start":108.3,"end":117.06,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Yeah, totally. Me too. They also help them learn new workplace skills, things like writing emails, that sort of thing."},{"start":117.06,"end":127.62,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"It does sound good, but offering things like workplace skills, isn't that just like any other job centre? What's this got to do with technology?"},{"start":128.44,"end":144.7,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Well, this one is special. The centres themselves are entirely cash free and young people who join can earn virtual money called imali, which means money in Zulu apparently. You can spend it there at the centre."},{"start":144.7,"end":149.24,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"So do they use computers to earn it, just like Bitcoin?"},{"start":149.78,"end":163.08,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"No, no. They earn this imali in lots of different ways. One of the things they can do is local volunteering and they can do any kind of volunteering as long as it's in the local area."},{"start":163.76,"end":173.68,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Like they might help out a nearby school or help the old people in the community. The other thing they can do is go to personal development workshops."},{"start":173.68,"end":180.88,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"So they earn for attending. Yeah, that's nice. And what do they learn about at these workshops?"},{"start":181.44,"end":188.52,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"You know, like how to not give up when you're dealing with a problem or how to set yourself goals, things like that."},{"start":188.9,"end":194.04,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"That sounds pretty cool. What can they buy with this? What's its name?"},{"start":194.66,"end":195.18,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Imali."},{"start":195.88,"end":207.54,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Imali. Well, as I said, the centres are cash free, but they can use imali at the centre cafes to buy things like snacks. They can also use the money to pay for online courses."},{"start":208.58,"end":211.12,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Can they work on the courses at home too?"},{"start":211.82,"end":217.8,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"I think so, but the centres have computers so apparently most people prefer to spend time there."},{"start":218.38,"end":223.04,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Sounds great. Anything else? I mean that they can buy with?"},{"start":223.04,"end":229.98,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Imali. Yeah, the other online option is that you can donate imalis to charity."},{"start":230.84,"end":235.28,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Does that mean the charity gets imalis? But how is that useful?"},{"start":235.78,"end":240.2,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"No, no, the Youth Boost Centre gives the charities real money."},{"start":241.72,"end":246.22,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"But members, they don't earn actual money, but they still like it?"},{"start":246.54,"end":247.3,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Apparently so."},{"start":247.76,"end":249.26,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"So what's the big attraction?"},{"start":249.72,"end":255.38,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Well, from what it said in the article, it's just a place where they can feel a sense of belonging."},{"start":255.86,"end":264.87,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Oh, that's really nice. Okay, so it would be good to write in the article what we think. Let's talk about the good points first."},{"start":266.01,"end":268.57,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Rachel, you were researching it. What do you reckon?"},{"start":269.11,"end":277.05,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"I think they're an excellent idea, mainly because they give people a way to give back to the community. So it's more than just basic welfare."},{"start":277.05,"end":280.79,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Yeah, I was thinking the same. What do you think, Aaron?"},{"start":281.59,"end":289.07,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"From what Rachel was saying, I think the best thing seems to be that it lets people learn life skills, like having to deal with money."},{"start":289.61,"end":295.65,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Alright. What about the cons? Can you see any downsides to this imali system?"},{"start":296.19,"end":300.85,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Well, the obvious problem that I can see is that actual money is more useful."},{"start":300.85,"end":307.79,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"People need real money to spend on meals, not just snacks, especially if they need to help their families."},{"start":308.39,"end":312.71,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Yes, that's a very good point. What about you, Aaron? What do you think?"},{"start":313.57,"end":318.09,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Well, again, from what Rachel said so far, it's hard to see any bad points."},{"start":318.91,"end":328.51,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Maybe the only downside I can think of would be it might be vulnerable to hacking. You know, because, well, someone could hack into it online."},{"start":330.5,"end":337.38,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"That is the end of task three. You now have one minute to tidy up your answers."},{"start":401.86,"end":401.9,"speaker":"Sarah, Rachel and Aaron","text":"Four. Sarah is interviewing Dr. James Berg, a computer specialist working with the NGO Tarako Solutions for the IT Club's online magazine."}],"4":[{"start":0,"end":13.68,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Four. Sarah is interviewing Dr. James Berg, a computer specialist working with the NGO Tarako Solutions for the IT Club's online magazine."},{"start":14.99,"end":24.06,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Listen to the interview and complete the answers below. Please note that you do not need to answer incomplete sentences."},{"start":25.57,"end":34.87,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have 30 seconds to study the task. At the end of the task, you will have three minutes to tidy up your answers."},{"start":66.66,"end":74.72,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Dr. Berg, thank you for taking the time to meet us today. Can you tell us a bit about the ideas behind Tarako Solutions?"},{"start":74.72,"end":84.64,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Certainly. Well, Tarako Solutions is an NGO, as you probably know, and we operate in poor and remote areas all over the world."},{"start":85.34,"end":90.46,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"We work in these areas to solve local problems, infrastructure problems mainly."},{"start":90.96,"end":96.18,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Oh, really? That's quite interesting. What kind of infrastructure problems?"},{"start":96.18,"end":107.3,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Well, maybe I can illustrate what we do with a recent redevelopment project in Thailand we were working on, where we built a new bus shelter for a group of commuters."},{"start":108.02,"end":112.8,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"This helped local people deal with an uncomfortable journey to work and school."},{"start":113.72,"end":117.26,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"And are the projects designed for special groups of people?"},{"start":117.26,"end":130.26,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Actually, it's the opposite. We really try to embrace diversity in everything we do, so we always try to invite, you know, people who are often overlooked in traditional society."},{"start":130.9,"end":134.76,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Very often it's these kind of people that don't get to have their say."},{"start":135.46,"end":137.36,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"OK, now I'd like..."},{"start":137.36,"end":145.34,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Sorry, I was going to add. When we're building things like the bus shelter, we invite ideas from the children,"},{"start":145.34,"end":148.3,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"as they are the users who are often overlooked."},{"start":149.49,"end":156.65,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Well, that all sounds very positive. I'd like to move on to how Tarako Solutions uses technology."},{"start":157.73,"end":161.81,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"You work with AR, augmented reality. Is that right?"},{"start":162.17,"end":167.05,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Yes, that's right. AR mixes digital elements with real life."},{"start":167.41,"end":168.93,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"It sounds quite technical."},{"start":168.93,"end":178.27,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"It's the same tech used in the game Pokemon Go, but instead of a monster, you can see things like a new bridge or a staircase."},{"start":179.29,"end":185.01,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"AR is great. I mean, we can literally see the designs as they would appear in real life."},{"start":185.75,"end":185.97,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Amazing!"},{"start":186.93,"end":193.39,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"And another thing about AR is that it lets other people see which final designs they like best."},{"start":193.39,"end":199.09,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"This is important because in order to choose the final design, we have a public vote."},{"start":200.09,"end":207.79,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Right. Now, AR is new to me, so I imagine it is probably a new concept for most of the people you're dealing with."},{"start":208.13,"end":209.59,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"So how do you deal with that?"},{"start":210.05,"end":218.77,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Well, that's a good point. Everybody who's selected to join the project must attend a three-day AR training programme."},{"start":219.25,"end":219.67,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"OK."},{"start":219.67,"end":226.89,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"And for some users, it's actually the first time they've ever used a computer, so it's an essential part of the process."},{"start":227.83,"end":231.07,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Can you tell us what your favourite project has been so far?"},{"start":231.59,"end":236.61,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Well, I think one of the most memorable developments has been the Kerala Project in India."},{"start":237.11,"end":238.97,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"OK, and what did that entail?"},{"start":239.41,"end":244.31,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Well, this was a project designed to improve a riverside path to a market."},{"start":244.31,"end":246.73,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"There were several things we had to address."},{"start":247.31,"end":253.39,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"We had to build in safety measures into the design to help deal with flash floods, for a start."},{"start":253.85,"end":254.69,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"That was important."},{"start":255.53,"end":261.91,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Plus, one special thing about this project was that the children who used the route gave us important information."},{"start":262.61,"end":270.87,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"They, the children, told us that actually the area had a problem with a lot of dangerous pests, especially snakes."},{"start":270.87,"end":274.43,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"So again, we built in features to deal with that."},{"start":274.95,"end":275.15,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Right."},{"start":275.93,"end":279.15,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"This project also taught us a lot about building trust."},{"start":279.97,"end":283.01,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"I mean, many of the locals were quite doubtful at first."},{"start":283.47,"end":284.67,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Did they explain why?"},{"start":285.01,"end":285.67,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Yes, they did."},{"start":286.13,"end":294.13,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"They told us about a similar project in the village a few years before that had been left unfinished and actually never was finished."},{"start":294.13,"end":301.57,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"So I suppose they would have been worried that the same thing might happen to your project, that it wouldn't be finished either."},{"start":302.09,"end":302.65,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Precisely."},{"start":303.38,"end":305.14,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Which I think is fair enough."},{"start":305.6,"end":307.6,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"I think it was a genuine concern."},{"start":308.44,"end":314.66,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"The other reason why they were quite doubtful about it all was to do with what would happen after we left."},{"start":315.2,"end":319.88,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"They were worried that there would be no one to maintain the path once we'd gone."},{"start":319.88,"end":324.74,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Again, another genuine worry. So how did you change their minds?"},{"start":325.44,"end":332.92,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Well, we had to convince them that we aren't just another temporary volunteer project, that we wouldn't just leave."},{"start":333.71,"end":342.35,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"What really helped was another piece of technology, one that could continue to support the Kerala project long after construction had finished."},{"start":343.05,"end":344.45,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Oh yeah? And what was that?"},{"start":344.45,"end":353.33,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Well, we set up webcams that deliver a live fee 24 hours a day on our webpage. It's a win-win for everyone."},{"start":353.89,"end":360.47,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"It means that for the local users we can easily see areas where the path had deteriorated."},{"start":361.47,"end":365.43,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"The webcams are great for that, so it's been a great success."},{"start":366.35,"end":371.67,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"And for Turaco Solutions, what were the benefits? You said it was a win-win situation."},{"start":371.67,"end":381.35,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"Oh yes, sorry. It also means that we at Turaco Solutions can get more funding as we promote our work online using the images."},{"start":382.05,"end":386.17,"speaker":"Sarah Lo and Dr James Berg","text":"OK. Thank you so much for telling us about Turaco Solutions today."}]},"partB":[{"start":0.05,"end":5.29,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Look at page 2 of your data file."},{"start":13.38,"end":27.31,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"You will listen to a recording of a video conference discussion between Ms. Myra Ray, the chair of the Interschool Visual Media Society, and Ringo Chow."},{"start":28.65,"end":31.31,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Take notes under the appropriate headings."},{"start":32.21,"end":46.65,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Before the recording is played, you will have five minutes to study the question answer book and the data file to familiarize yourself with the situation and the tasks."},{"start":48.88,"end":56.16,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Complete the tasks by following the instructions in the question answer book and on the recording."},{"start":56.83,"end":66.19,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"You will find all the information you need in the question answer book, the data file, and on the recording."},{"start":67.89,"end":73.57,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"As you listen, you can make notes on page 3 of the data file."},{"start":75.12,"end":82.68,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have five minutes to familiarize yourself with the question answer book and the data file."},{"start":82.68,"end":391.66,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"The recording is about to begin. Turn to page 3 of the data file."},{"start":423.28,"end":424.58,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah, I agree."},{"start":430.66,"end":436,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"And the entries for the short video competition? How are the entries coming along?"},{"start":436.82,"end":440.3,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Not great. We've only had three entries so far."},{"start":440.6,"end":440.86,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Oh."},{"start":441.74,"end":449.3,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah. As we said in the committee meeting, Mod needs to change the design of the poster to try to encourage more entries."},{"start":449.3,"end":458.9,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yes. I was thinking a bit more about Mod's poster design. I noticed that the website is on the poster, but it's the wrong one."},{"start":459.34,"end":459.5,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Really?"},{"start":460,"end":462.9,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yes. We changed the URL. Remember?"},{"start":463.58,"end":466.7,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Oh, yes. Is it still the old one on the poster?"},{"start":467.2,"end":467.6,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah."},{"start":468.32,"end":474.1,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Oh, I didn't notice. Can you give it to me again? Nico will need it to tell Mod."},{"start":474.91,"end":480.94,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"It's www.isvms.hk"},{"start":480.94,"end":490.86,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Okay. Just to make sure, it's www.isvms.hk, right?"},{"start":491.16,"end":492.44,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yes. That's right."},{"start":492.64,"end":493.14,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Okay."},{"start":493.74,"end":498.94,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"And something else I just thought of. Did Mod put a QR code on the poster?"},{"start":500.05,"end":500.33,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Sorry?"},{"start":501.12,"end":503.59,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Did she put a QR code on the poster?"},{"start":504.53,"end":508,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"The QR code? I don't know. I'll need to check."},{"start":508.78,"end":513.74,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Well, make sure the QR code's on the bottom left-hand corner of the poster."},{"start":514.64,"end":519.56,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Sure. I'll make a note of that. Bottom left-hand corner."},{"start":520.48,"end":525.16,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Now, you say only three people have entered the competition so far?"},{"start":525.16,"end":533.1,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah. It's a bit disappointing. Actually, I was wondering whether we should extend the deadline to the 13th of May."},{"start":533.96,"end":541.9,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"You want to extend the deadline to the 13th of May? Are you sure? But isn't 13 an unlucky number?"},{"start":542.86,"end":544.66,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Don't be so superstitious."},{"start":545.26,"end":551.04,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Okay. Let's go with the 13th then. We will have to change it on the poster as well."},{"start":551.42,"end":551.76,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Okay."},{"start":551.76,"end":560,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Anyway, bad stuff does happen on the 13th. Isabel Luna, you know, the director of the electronic durian?"},{"start":560.26,"end":560.56,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah."},{"start":560.98,"end":564.76,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Well, she had her skateboarding accident on the 13th."},{"start":565.78,"end":566.88,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Well, there you go then."},{"start":567.4,"end":571.66,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Right. Let's move on to the next thing. The Bright House Cinema."},{"start":572.59,"end":579.61,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"As you will remember from the meeting last week, the committee are still keen for us to choose the Bright House for the screening."},{"start":580.23,"end":584.83,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"And Alia is going to do a site visit of Bright House Cinema tomorrow."},{"start":586.19,"end":592.09,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Sorry. Wait. You say that Isabel Luna's had an accident? That's the first I've heard."},{"start":592.95,"end":595.81,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"I mean, does it mean she won't be able to come to the screening?"},{"start":596.39,"end":604.05,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"No, no. She's still coming to the screening. But it was quite serious, I think. I mean, she's in a wheelchair."},{"start":604.83,"end":608.75,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Really? And will that be a problem for the Bright House?"},{"start":608.75,"end":610.49,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"The wheelchair, I mean."},{"start":611.41,"end":616.25,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yes. Well, that's what we will find out from Alia's report on her site visit."},{"start":616.75,"end":622.61,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"And that's why we stipulated wheelchair access to the stage in the venue requirements."},{"start":623.41,"end":626.13,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Oh, yeah. I did wonder why we put that."},{"start":627.07,"end":633.91,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah. Well, obviously, if she's in a wheelchair, we will need a ramp to get her on to the stage for the discussion after the screening."},{"start":635.44,"end":638.52,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"I mean, the Bright House is a terrible cinema."},{"start":638.52,"end":646.68,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yes. You don't need to tell me. And there's something else that I'm worried about that we didn't discuss in the committee meeting."},{"start":647.18,"end":648,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"What's that then?"},{"start":648.68,"end":656.78,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Well, you remember that the big thing about the screening of the electronic durian is that the audience will be wearing those 3D headsets?"},{"start":657.24,"end":657.9,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah, yeah."},{"start":657.9,"end":669.1,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"So, it will be critical on the night that handing out the 3D headsets to the audience is done quickly. Otherwise, it will take far too long and it'll delay everything."},{"start":669.94,"end":675.93,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah. Otherwise, it could end up being a nightmare. I'd say we'll need at least 10 ushers."},{"start":676.47,"end":679.93,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yes. That's what I thought. At least 10 ushers."},{"start":680.54,"end":689.48,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"I talked to Alia and she'll find out how many ushers Bright House has when she does the site visit tomorrow. And I'm sure it won't be 10."},{"start":690.64,"end":695.62,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"And there's another thing that I'm worried about at the Bright House to do with the noodles."},{"start":696.57,"end":697.61,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"What do you mean noodles?"},{"start":698.25,"end":708.55,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Well, you remember that we decided that we're going to bring noodles to give out to the audience to eat during the showing of the electronic durian. You know, in the metal noodles scene."},{"start":708.55,"end":711.35,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah, yeah. The metal noodles scene."},{"start":711.99,"end":723.13,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah. Well, I'm now worried that the Bright House won't let us. I've told Alia to ask the manager at the Bright House tomorrow if we will be allowed to bring in outside food."},{"start":724.03,"end":726.11,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"I can imagine what they'll say."},{"start":726.43,"end":737.51,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah, I know. The noodles are supposed to be one of our key fun elements of the evening. Having all these people eat noodles while watching the metal noodles scene."},{"start":737.51,"end":744.61,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"I still think it'll be hilarious. All these people trying to eat noodles with their 3D headsets on."},{"start":745.29,"end":749.57,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"I agree. It would be a big loss for the whole event if they don't let us."},{"start":750.01,"end":752.43,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Well, let's wait and see what they say."},{"start":753.03,"end":763.99,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah, right. Moving on. The other thing that we need to discuss is the prize-giving ceremony. Is there any news on the venue for the prize-giving ceremony?"},{"start":763.99,"end":772.93,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"The prize-giving ceremony? Oh, yes. I just got confirmation today. We got the Cultural Plaza in Central."},{"start":773.55,"end":788.19,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Oh, great. So we got the Cultural Plaza after all. I always said the Cultural Plaza was the best choice. It's an amazing venue and a location. I mean Central such a convenient location compared to the other ones."},{"start":788.91,"end":791.09,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"And the date? Has the date been finalized?"},{"start":791.09,"end":795.07,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yes. It's Saturday, June the 22nd."},{"start":795.71,"end":799.19,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Wait a second. Let me just note that down. When was that?"},{"start":800.03,"end":802.09,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"June the 22nd."},{"start":802.53,"end":805.69,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Okay. And the time? When will it start?"},{"start":806.23,"end":809.91,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Um, let me check. Half past seven."},{"start":810.35,"end":813.31,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Okay, seven thirty. Right."},{"start":814.01,"end":815.69,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Anything else that we need to discuss?"},{"start":816.39,"end":823.79,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah. The other thing I wanted to bring up was the introductory speech. You know, the one on the current state of cinema."},{"start":824.19,"end":828.51,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Oh, yeah. The one that Nico will give to introduce the discussion."},{"start":828.99,"end":833.29,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah. I think Nico's struggling a bit for ideas, to tell you the truth."},{"start":833.29,"end":848.69,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Well, I think talk about two things. Film viewing habits. I mean, whether people watch films at home or go to the cinema nowadays, and also talk about low-budget films compared to, like, blockbusters."},{"start":849.57,"end":856.33,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Right. Yeah, that sounds good. So what could Nico say about watching films at home or at the cinema?"},{"start":856.95,"end":862.05,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Well, you remember that I went to the screening of the electronic durian the other night."},{"start":862.05,"end":862.65,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah?"},{"start":863.27,"end":870.73,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Well, I was thinking. These 3D headsets. You know, those 360-degree headsets?"},{"start":871.23,"end":872.19,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"The Janus ones?"},{"start":872.57,"end":884.99,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Exactly. Well, they are absolutely fantastic and everything. But it struck me. I could have exactly the same experience sitting at home in my living room on my sofa and…"},{"start":884.99,"end":888.73,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Never need to go to the cinema. Yeah, I thought that as well."},{"start":888.73,"end":892.31,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"There's no point going to the cinema. Just stay at home."},{"start":893.33,"end":897.55,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Okay. And what could Nico say about low-budget films and blockbusters?"},{"start":898.13,"end":910.61,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Well, I was thinking. In the last decade or so, big studios have tended to focus more and more of their resources on making expensive blockbusters for the cinema so that they…"},{"start":910.61,"end":912.35,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Can make bigger profits."},{"start":912.35,"end":929.21,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Exactly. Because a studio knows that if it puts all its energy into making one successful blockbuster, like Star Wars or a Marvel superhero film, the bottom line is it'll make bigger profits."},{"start":929.41,"end":930.11,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah, I know."},{"start":930.11,"end":943.83,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"And these blockbusters, the studio's launch absolutely enormous multi-million dollar advertising and marketing campaigns, and small low-budget filmmakers simply cannot compete with all that."},{"start":943.97,"end":945.27,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah, I know."},{"start":945.73,"end":956.55,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"If Nico could say all that in the introductory speech and maybe add something a bit more optimistic as well, so it's not all doom and gloom, that would be great."},{"start":957.05,"end":959.27,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Yeah, okay. I'll pass on your message."},{"start":961.62,"end":965.66,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"That is the end of the listening component of this paper."},{"start":966.62,"end":977.04,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"You will now have one hour and fifteen minutes to complete the written task in either Part B1 or Part B2."},{"start":978.16,"end":980.92,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"An announcement will be made when time is up."},{"start":982.6,"end":986.06,"speaker":"Visual Media Society call","text":"Take off your earphones now and turn off the radio."}]});})();
